    "q-137890": {
      "dom_id": "step-q137890",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the solution for the weighted least-squares problem $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 27 \\\\ 27\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "To get the normal equation corresponding to $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ we pre-multiply both sides of the equation by $(W\\,A)^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot W\\,Ax & =(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot Wb \\\\ {A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)Ax & ={A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n{W}^{T}W=[\\begin{aligned}{5}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {2}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {2}^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}25 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nour normal equation can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}25 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}25 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 27 \\\\ 27\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 25 \\\\ -4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 108 \\\\ 108\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 29\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 108\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the matrix on the left-hand side is invertible, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & ={[\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 29\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 108\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8\\cdot 29-4\\cdot 4}[\\begin{aligned}29 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 108\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{216}[\\begin{aligned}-432 \\\\ 864\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
